    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`). The audit line in the run confirms the behavior end-to-end:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2616E6609E9\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\n         \"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"schemaVersion\":2,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n`memberId` carries the `V2` tag, `ownerSegment` is `STANDARD_METRO` (plain region \u2192 METRO, no tag leak), and `schemaVersion` is 2.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity, in one place.** New `model/IdentityVersion` holds the single source of truth: `NUMBER = 2` (used for both `apiVersion` and `schemaVersion`) and `TAG = \"V2\"` (mixed into every identifier).\n\n**The region code inside the identifiers.** `RegionResolver.identityRegionFor(postcode, city)` returns `\"V2\" + regionFor(...)`. `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` now feeds this to the member-id generator, so the region embedded in `memberId` is version-tagged.\n\n**Each identifier now differs from v1:**\n- `memberId` \u2014 region segment becomes the `V2`-tagged code (`ClinicServiceImpl`).\n- `householdId` \u2014 `HouseholdIdGenerator` mixes the fixed `V2` tag into the hash input (kept a *constant* tag, not the region, so same-lastname+postcode owners still share a household).\n- `identityKey` \u2014 `Owner.getIdentityKey()` prepends the `V2` tag to the hash input.\n\n**Decoupled user-facing fields from the (now opaque, tagged) member id.** `Owner.getLocality()` and `getFiscalYear()` now derive straight from the owner's own postcode/city and registration date via `RegionResolver`/`FiscalYear`, so `locality` stays the plain `\"NSW\"`, `timezone` and the owner segment's region stay plain. This made `MemberId.regionOf`/`fiscalYearShortOf` dead (they couldn't parse a tagged region anyway), so I removed them.\n\n**Response shape.** In `openapi.yml`: added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema (`memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`), added a top-level integer `apiVersion` and an `identity` ref on `Owner`, and removed the three flat identifier fields. `OwnerMapper` builds the nested `identity` object and sets `apiVersion` from `IdentityVersion.NUMBER`.\n\n**Audit schema v2.** `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained `schemaVersion` (= `IdentityVersion.NUMBER`) and the recomputed `ownerSegment`; `OwnerAuditLogger` passes the owner's segment through.\n\nLogic stayed in its natural home: version constants in `IdentityVersion`, region derivation in `RegionResolver`, each identifier's hashing in its own generator / `Owner` getter, response shaping in the mapper/OpenAPI spec, and audit shape in the event record.",
