    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners` (handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:182`).\n\n## Before the method body runs (framework-level, in order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected.\n2. **Bean Validation of the request body** \u2014 the interface is `@Validated` and the body is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnersApi.java:91`). The DTO constraints are enforced:\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max = 10)`\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(max = 255)`\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max = 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max = 255)`\n\n## Inside `addOwner` (in order)\n\n3. **Idempotency replay check** \u2014 `replayIdempotentCreate(idempotencyKey)`. If the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before and its owner still exists, that original owner is returned with `200 OK` and **all steps below are skipped** (no new owner, no side-effects).\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)`.\n5. **Address normalization + presence validation** \u2014 `normalizeAddress(owner)` mutates the owner: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/flat `address`, prefers the structured line 1 (composing it into `address`) else the flat address. If neither a structured nor flat address is present \u2192 **400 Bad Request**.\n6. **Telephone validation/normalization** \u2014 `telephoneNormalizer.toE164(...)`. If not a valid phone number \u2192 **400**. (Normalized E.164 value held for later.)\n7. **Email validation** \u2014 `emailNormalizer.normalize(...)`; if non-null and either invalid or from a disposable/blocklisted domain \u2192 **400**.\n8. **Postcode validation** \u2014 if postcode is non-null and `postcodeValidator.isValid(postcode, city)` fails \u2192 **400**.\n9. **Registration-date-not-in-future validation** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after today \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Registration date side-effect** \u2014 compute `BusinessDay.rollForward(supplied date, or today if none)` and set it on the owner.\n11. **Per-day cap validation** \u2014 if `countOwnersByRegistrationDate(registrationDate) >= 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n12. **Apply normalized contact fields** \u2014 set the E.164 `telephone` and normalized `email` on the owner.\n13. **Per-city cap validation** \u2014 if `countOwnersByCity(city) >= 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n14. **Hard-duplicate validation** \u2014 `isDuplicateOwner(owner)` (live owner sharing normalized telephone, email, and phonetic/Soundex last name). If matched \u2192 **409 Conflict**. (Note the disposable-email 400 in step 7 takes precedence over this.)\n15. **Declared-household flag side-effect** \u2014 `owner.setDeclaredHouseholdMember(sharesHousehold == true)`.\n16. **Persist via `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** (transactional), which for a new owner stamps, in order:\n    - **`memberId`** \u2014 generated uniquely from region (postcode/city), fiscal short-year of registration date, telephone, and last name.\n    - **`namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n    - **`bulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 true if owners already registered that date exceed the bulk-signup threshold.\n    - **`capacityWarning`** \u2014 true if the city\u2019s owner count is at/above the city-capacity warning threshold.\n    - **`householdId`** \u2014 derived from last name + postcode.\n    - **`householdSize`** \u2014 existing owners sharing that household id, plus one.\n    - **`membershipLevelCap`** \u2014 one above the highest membership level among existing household members (null if none).\n    - **`possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 soft-duplicate detection (same phonetic last name + postcode, different identity key; skipped if declared household member or no postcode); records presence and the earliest matching owner\u2019s id.\n    - **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 the actual DB insert.\n17. **Audit logging** \u2014 `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` writes an `AUDIT` log line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) plus a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (with an incrementing sequence, primary identifier, owner segment).\n18. **Welcome notification** \u2014 `welcomeNotifier.welcome(owner)` emits a `NOTIFY` log entry (id, memberId).\n19. **Idempotency record** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, `idempotencyStore.remember(key, owner.getId())` (first writer wins).\n20. **Response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\nA note on ordering nuance: steps 3\u201315 are validations/mutations that can short-circuit the request (with the HTTP status shown); steps 16\u201320 are the actual creation side-effects and only run once every validation has passed."
